All in all, the PC overlay version is highly playable, and on my
reasonably fast (SI 20.3) machine, playing from a ramdisk, the
action of the overlays is transparent, but playing on a slow hard
disk I was quite miffed when, having restored an old game, I died
within a few moves. I hit the 'l' key, nothing happened, hit it again,
a bit harder, still nowt, again, lurch 3 squares, straight into the
middle of a morgue - instant death. It's too much to expect me to
glance at the drive LED before every move, so...

Please, try to clear the keyboard queue whenever new overlays are
loaded, maybe as a .cfg option - this quirk also occurs on multi-
tasking UNIX when things are busy, (with the tape drive running) it
can be 10-15 seconds before my next move gets played. I don't expect
a cure for UNIX, but single tasking, single user can accomodate a
simple fix.

I still can't get as far as I did in 2.x. but I'm not complaining!

Happy Christmas all!

Dave E.


